{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787222698,"nonce":"dopKBAfpmjwOG+SAU8NwmJAX2cM=","message":"Done, per **comment #1** — the body is false and was not implemented.\n\n**Built, not swapped.** The affordance did not exist: `ViewService.actions` emitted only `oto.unack`,\n`oto.ack`, `oto.noop.runbook`, `oto.noop.silence`, and there was zero `oto.snooze` in the tree.\n\n**Neither overflow nor modal — a `static_select`.** `overflowMenu` is documented links-only and already\nat its five-option ceiling, and a second bare overflow would have put two visually identical `…` menus\nin one row, one of which changes oto's behaviour. A modal needs `views.open` with `trigger_id` on\n§H.8's 3-second synchronous path — the exact thing the `Handle`/`Apply` split exists to keep off it —\nplus an interaction type `parseSlackEnvelope` refuses by design. A select carries its own placeholder,\nso the row stays self-describing, and its option ceiling is 100.\n\n**Presets:** `30m · 1h · 4h · 24h · 7d`, from SPEC §B.8.3 and corroborated by §P-17. No indefinite\noption. All five inside the 5 min–30 day bounds.\n\n**Wiring.** `ActionSnooze`/`ActionUnsnooze` added to the closed set in `channels/service/interactions.go`;\na new `Snoozes` port; handlers branch onto `Service.SnoozeAs`/`UnsnoozeAs` (`alerts/service/seam.go` —\nthe ticket's `internal/grouping` citation had drifted, that package is deleted). `interaction_payload.go`\nnow reads `selected_option.value`: **without it every menu press arrives blank**, because Slack sends\nbutton payloads under `value` and menu payloads elsewhere. The snoozed card offers `:bell: Unsnooze`\ninstead of Snooze, off the `SnoozedUntil` already on the view. Goldens `root_snoozed` / `root_unsnoozed`\npin both states.\n\n⚠️ **It shipped inert once and was caught in review:** the adapter was missing, so the port was nil and\nevery press answered with an honest \"not in this deployment yet\" ephemeral. `slackSnoozeActions` now\nexists in `app/adapters.go`, is injected in `container.go`, and has a compile-time assertion in\n`assertions.go` — that assertion earns its line precisely because the port is optional, so drift would\nsilently revert the menu to the ephemeral rather than failing a build.\n\n**Known limitation, not fixed:** idempotency is the unkeyed zero value, and `alerts/service.Snooze`\nalways supersedes, so a Slack interaction retry (Slack retries on a slow ack) writes a duplicate\n`unsnoozed(superseded)` + `snoozed` event pair in the timeline. Worth a follow-up ticket; nothing in\n`Handle` reads `X-Slack-Retry-Num`.\n\nAlso surfaced, pre-existing and separate: `oto.more` matches neither the closed set nor `oto.noop.`, so\nevery links-overflow press already lands in the unknown-action counter. Not caused here.\n\nSPEC §H.7's limit moved 4 → 5 to seat the select; authorised by **ADR 0043**, written for it.","files":null}]}